--- !u!114 &8660679313131249169
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In the image above, another lighting sampling artifact is visible due to the different <b>Subdivision Levels</b> encountered in this room. In this particular scenario, increasing the <b>Sampling Noise,</b> as seen in the previous step, was not considered because it may cause unwanted leaking artifacts.\n\nThankfully, we can prevent these artifacts by adding a Local <b> Probe Volume</b> in the Scene, forcing the <b>Probe Spacing</b> to be fixed, and enabling the <b>Fill Empty Spaces</b> property. This way, we can enforce uniform spacing between all probes. \n\nWith no additional <b>Subdivision Levels</b> in this local <b> Probe Volume,</b> more probes are created. Therefore, the baking time and the amount of data on disk will slightly increase.\n\n\nTo reproduce the artifact seen in the image above, follow these steps:\n\n1. Add a Cube at <b>X:25.3 Y:2 Z:1.5</b>\n\n2. In the <i>Hierarchy</i> window, select <b>Lighting</b> > <b>Probe Volumes</b> > <b>Probe Volume Local.</b>\n\nYou can notice in the <i>Inspector</i> that the range slider has its Min and Max value set at 0.6 m, and that the <b>Fill Empty Spaces</b> property is enabled, to ensure a fixed spacing for all probes.\n\n4. Disable the <b>Probe Volume Local</b> GameObject and save the scene.\n\n5. Click the <b>Generate Lighting</b> button at the bottom of the <i>Lighting</i> window to rebake the lighting.\n\nThe sampling artifact will appear on the Cube.\n\n6. Re-enable the <b>Probe Volume Local</b> GameObject and regenerate the lighting to fix the issue again."
